        r"""<p>The temporal behavior of these stationary configurations is resolved by applying the unitary operator that generates translations in time. This dynamic mapping is governed by the <strong>Time Evolution</strong> operator \( \hat{U}(t) = e^{-i\hat{H}t/\hbar} \), which acts on the spatial states to generate their temporal phase evolution. The Time-Independent Schrödinger Equation is formulated as"""
